text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edge position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":" is incidence number "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, and within a hyperedge in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)"},{"type":"text","text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a per-incidence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array must be rebuilt for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"text":" it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traversal"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Connectivity"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPaths"},{"text":" and the rest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidentIndexRows"},{"text":" writes the view’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidenceRows"},{"text":", in O(n + m + p), for whole-graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range, O(1). On ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"text":", which stores its incidences, every read is O(1) plus","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the row. On any other base, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"text":" binary-search the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hyperedge and find the member by its rank (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)"},{"text":"), O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"text":" finds its place in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"text":", which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them on a base without a faster ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraphView, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the bipartite structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the view’s components restricted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"type":"text","text":" are the hypergraph’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView/endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)":{"title":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The incidence’s vertex index and n plus its hyperedge index, without hashing: two loads on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a binary search and a walk of the hyperedge’s members otherwise."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"endpointIndices","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofEdgeAt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> (u","kind":"text"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", v","kind":"text"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/endpointindices(ofedgeat:)"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView/degree(ofIndex:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/degree(ofindex:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"key